-    # The trigger phrase alone is not authorisation: on a public repository
-    # anyone can write `@claude` in a comment, and this job checks out the
-    # head, runs with `contents: write` and holds an API key. The association
-    # test is what makes the trigger a request from someone who already has
-    # write access. Both events this workflow listens to carry
-    # `github.event.comment.author_association`; adding an event without one
-    # means adding its own test here. GitHub's association values are
-    # documented at
-    # https://docs.github.com/en/graphql/reference/enums#commentauthorassociation
-    # (read 2026-09-02).
-    #
-    # Two caveats, so nobody reads this gate as stronger than it is. `MEMBER`
-    # means organisation membership, not write access. `COLLABORATOR` is
-    # weaker still: GitHub assigns it to anyone *invited* to the repository,
-    # including read-only and triage-only collaborators - so an invitee who
-    # cannot push can nonetheless start a job holding the API key and
-    # `contents: write`. Acceptable for a repository with no collaborators,
-    # and a decision to revisit the day one is added: narrow to `OWNER`, or
-    # gate on a maintainers team.
-    if: github.event_name == 'workflow_dispatch'
+    needs: gate
     runs-on: ubuntu-latest
     timeout-minutes: 30
+    # DP-039 (b).5 - the key is an environment secret of `claude`, the only
+    # environment line in this file. "If the environment requires approval, a
+    # job cannot access environment secrets until one of the required
+    # reviewers approves it" ([GH-ENV], Environment secrets). The owner's
+    # settings (work order 16 §3 item 8): create the environment; name its
+    # reviewer; set its deployment rule to "selected branches" with the
+    # default branch only and no tag pattern; store ANTHROPIC_API_KEY there and
+    # NOT as a repository secret, which every job could read (check that
+    # `gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/actions/secrets` does not list it). Required
+    # reviewers exist on Free/Pro/Team plans only for public repositories
+    # ([GH-ENV]). Leave "Prevent self-review" off while the owner is the only
+    # reviewer, or nobody can approve the owner's own dispatch.
+    environment: claude
